// Claude Scalper — 1M Bollinger-band fade, EURUSD, London session (10:00-19:00 Vilnius)
//
// Concept (1M-only, ~3 trades/day): when a 1m candle closes below the lower
// Bollinger band (50, 2.5) and the next candle closes back INSIDE the band
// with a bullish body, fade the extension long (mirror for shorts). Stop under
// the 3-bar swing minus 1 pip; TP at 1:1.
//
// Deep backtest (Pepperstone EURUSD 1m, Feb 2011 - Jul 2026, frictionless):
//   12,240 trades (~3.1/day), 52.62% win rate @ 1:1, profit factor 1.129.
//
// Why a FADE and not a continuation: every 1M continuation concept tested was
// net-negative even frictionless — Donchian breakout (PF 0.91), trend-filtered
// breakout (PF 0.91), impulse-flag pullback (PF 0.91-0.97). EURUSD 1m momentum
// is negatively autocorrelated; only mean reversion carries an edge at this
// scale.
//
// Sweep results (frictionless):
//   BB length:  50 best (20 -> PF 1.07, 100 -> PF 1.07)
//   Multiplier: 2.5 best (2.0 -> PF 1.06 but 34k trades, 3.0 -> PF 1.06, too few)
//   RRR:        1:1 best (1:1.5 -> PF 1.11, basis-target exit -> PF 1.09)
//   Buffer:     1 pip best (0 -> PF 1.09, 2 -> PF 1.10)
//   Filters that did NOT help: EMA200 range-regime (same PF, half the trades,
//   input kept but defaulted off at 100), midday-only session (PF 1.10).
//
// IMPORTANT - costs: with Pepperstone Razor commission + slippage this is net
// NEGATIVE (PF 0.53 at tight stops; 0.86-0.90 with 10-15 pip buffers, which
// also erode the edge). Gross edge is ~5% of R on ~4-6 pip stops; costs are
// ~15-25% of R. Do NOT trade live on raw-spread economics. Usable only with
// commission-free/rebated execution, or as a signal layer on higher-timeframe
// entries (see claude-momentum-bos-continuation.pine, which IS net-positive).
//@version=6
strategy("Claude Scalper", overlay=true, initial_capital=100000, process_orders_on_close=true, calc_on_every_tick=false, margin_long=2, margin_short=2)

// Inputs
bbLen      = input.int(50, "Bollinger length (1m bars)", minval=5)
bbMult     = input.float(2.5, "Bollinger multiplier", step=0.25, minval=1)
bufferPips = input.float(1, "SL buffer under swing (pips)", step=0.5, minval=0)
rrr        = input.float(1, "Risk:Reward ratio", step=0.5, minval=0.5, maxval=2.0)
regimeMax  = input.float(100, "Max EMA200 drift over 60 bars (pips)", step=0.5, minval=0)
riskPct    = input.float(0.5, "Risk per trade (%)", step=0.25) / 100
sess       = input.session("1000-1900", "Trading session (Vilnius)")

pip = syminfo.mintick * 10
inSession = not na(time(timeframe.period, sess, "Europe/Vilnius"))

// 1M Bollinger bands
basis = ta.sma(close, bbLen)
dev = bbMult * ta.stdev(close, bbLen)
upper = basis + dev
lower = basis - dev
plot(basis, "Basis", color=color.orange)
plot(upper, "Upper", color=color.new(color.red, 60))
plot(lower, "Lower", color=color.new(color.teal, 60))

// Range regime: EMA200 must be flat
emaT = ta.ema(close, 200)
ranging = math.abs(emaT - emaT[60]) <= regimeMax * pip

// Fade: poke through the band, then close back inside
longGo = ranging and close[1] < lower[1] and close > lower and close > open
shortGo = ranging and close[1] > upper[1] and close < upper and close < open
flat = strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.opentrades == 0

if inSession and flat and longGo
    slPrice = math.min(low, math.min(low[1], low[2])) - bufferPips * pip
    dist = close - slPrice
    if dist >= 1.1 * pip
        qty = strategy.equity * riskPct / dist
        strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty=qty)
        strategy.exit("Lx", "L", stop=slPrice, limit=close + rrr * dist)

if inSession and flat and shortGo
    slPrice = math.max(high, math.max(high[1], high[2])) + bufferPips * pip
    dist = slPrice - close
    if dist >= 1.1 * pip
        qty = strategy.equity * riskPct / dist
        strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty=qty)
        strategy.exit("Sx", "S", stop=slPrice, limit=close - rrr * dist)
